CODEBASE CONVENTIONS FOR GOTRANSIT:

This is a Next.js project with TypeScript. The checkout flow is in src/components/pages/CheckoutPage. Forms use react-hook-form for state management and validation, often combined with joi validators. Validation runs both client-side and on API routes (pages/api/*).

Email fields in forms use react-hook-form registration and validation rules. Look for:
- .toLowerCase() or .toUpperCase() calls on email values
- Email validation via joi schema (joi.string().email())
- Email comparison operations in form handlers or API routes
- Confirmation email sending logic

Test coverage is expected in src/components/pages/CheckoutPage/__tests__/CheckoutForm.spec.tsx. Extend this existing spec file rather than creating new test files. Use Jest's test patterns already established there.

Pre-commit hooks via husky will validate:
- Branch name matches ^(feature|bugfix|tech|release|hotfix)/[a-zA-Z0-9.-]+(/[a-z0-9-]+)?$
- Commit message passes commitlint

Watch for case-sensitivity issues in:
- Email field normalization (trim/lower/upper logic)
- Email comparison in validation or submission handlers
- Email state stored in form or Redux
- Email passed to confirmation endpoints or auth functions (next-auth)
- Test assertions that compare email strings
